**Read:** [Production of Chlor-alkali, BREF CAK](../sources/Chlor-Alkali-Production-BREF.lingua#r_69QNQ29VT4NA2MXHTVWDNP8T2W), the entire product conditioning, storage and loading treatment; [Production of Speciality Inorganic Chemicals, BREF SIC](../sources/Speciality-Inorganic-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_04G7NFYXE76QCB3DXCRJC1FSCP), the complete relevant product handling and quality context; [Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC](../sources/Organic-Fine-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K), the whole applicable product isolation, storage and multipurpose-material history.

A chemical transfer moves a material with a particular amount, composition, phase, history and uncertainty. Record those properties at the boundary actually used, including water, density, pressure/temperature, contamination and time where consequential. A mass, volume or certificate without its basis can describe a different quantity than a downstream user assumes.

Storage and packaging can alter water/gas uptake, degradation, particle state, inhibitor concentration or contact-derived impurities. A container's previous contents, cleaning and service state can matter. A product sampled at one point is not automatically unchanged at its later point of use.

Close inventories and distinguish measured loss, reaction, phase change, sampling difference and account error. Trace returned containers, recovered material, residual heel, wash and off-specification product. A useful handoff carries the evidence another party needs to interpret and continue the chemical work.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public storage/transfer interface for a chemical product, with actual measurement and material-compatibility evidence. Independently compare dispatched/received quantities and quality on compatible bases. Explain the observations needed to distinguish an actual material change from a sampling/calibration difference and propose a justified transfer arrangement that preserves the required useful state.

**Continue:** [Trace chemical constituents through wastewater collection, treatment and recovery](../environment/Wastewater-speciation-collection-treatment-and-returned-water.lingua#r_4GAQKC90SG8M9C30PYNMP86KSH).

